chx:X_HalvingEvery210000 a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:HalvingEvery210000 ; rdfs:label "four halvings on real blocks"@en ; skos:definition "The subsidy is 50 coins shifted right by one bit for every 210,000 blocks: blocks 210,000, 420,000, 630,000 and 840,000 were mined on 2012-11-28, 2016-07-09, 2020-05-11 and 2024-04-20 and carry 25, 12.5, 6.25 and 3.125 coins, each half of the block before it, and the interval is the constant nSubsidyHalvingInterval of 210,000."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_HalvingEvery210000 a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); hs = {n: L.jload('mempool_block_%d.json' % n) for n in (210000, 420000, 630000, 840000)}; ([(n, L.iso(b['timestamp'])[:10], L.subsidy(n) / 1e8, L.subsidy(n - 1) / 1e8) for n, b in hs.items()], L.const('core_src_kernel_chainparams.cpp', 'consensus.nSubsidyHalvingInterval'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'precisely every 210,000 blocks')) evaluates to ([(210000, '2012-11-28', 25.0, 50.0), (420000, '2016-07-09', 12.5, 25.0), (630000, '2020-05-11', 6.25, 12.5), (840000, '2024-04-20', 3.125, 6.25)], '210000', True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); hs = {n: L.jload('mempool_block_%d.json' % n) for n in (210000, 420000, 630000, 840000)}; ([(n, L.iso(b['timestamp'])[:10], L.subsidy(n) / 1e8, L.subsidy(n - 1) / 1e8) for n, b in hs.items()], L.const('core_src_kernel_chainparams.cpp', 'consensus.nSubsidyHalvingInterval'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'precisely every 210,000 blocks'))" ; chx:output "([(210000, '2012-11-28', 25.0, 50.0), (420000, '2016-07-09', 12.5, 25.0), (630000, '2020-05-11', 6.25, 12.5), (840000, '2024-04-20', 3.125, 6.25)], '210000', True)" .
chx:X_HalvingEvery210000 rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_HalvingEvery210000 .
chx:X_TotalSupplyBelow21Million a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TotalSupplyBelow21Million ; rdfs:label "the last satoshi at block 6,929,999"@en ; skos:definition "Summing the 33 non-zero rewards in whole satoshis gives 2,099,999,997,690,000 satoshis, 2,310,000 satoshis (0.0231 coins) short of 21 million coins; the last block with a reward of 1 satoshi is 6,929,999 and block 6,930,000 has none, about the year 2140, because the code shifts an integer."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_TotalSupplyBelow21Million a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.total_supply(), 2100000000000000 - L.total_supply(), L.subsidy(33 * 210000 - 1), L.subsidy(33 * 210000), 33 * 210000 - 1, L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'approximately the year 2140'), L.has('core_src_validation.cpp', 'nSubsidy >>= halvings')) evaluates to (2099999997690000, 2310000, 1, 0, 6929999, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.total_supply(), 2100000000000000 - L.total_supply(), L.subsidy(33 * 210000 - 1), L.subsidy(33 * 210000), 33 * 210000 - 1, L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'approximately the year 2140'), L.has('core_src_validation.cpp', 'nSubsidy >>= halvings'))" ; chx:output "(2099999997690000, 2310000, 1, 0, 6929999, True, True)" .
chx:X_TotalSupplyBelow21Million rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TotalSupplyBelow21Million .
chx:X_BookScriptFloatErratum a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:BookScriptFloatErratum ; rdfs:label "a script that prints 2100000000000000.0"@en ; skos:definition "The script max_money.py of the book divides the reward with current_reward /= 2, which is a float division in Python 3, so run as printed it goes on halving into fractions for 1,107 steps until the float underflows to zero and prints 2100000000000000.0 and not the 2099999997690000 of the book; with the integer division //= the result of the book appears."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_BookScriptFloatErratum a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.book_script_as_printed(), L.total_supply(), L.has('book_code_max_money.py', 'current_reward /= 2'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', '2099999997690000')) evaluates to (2100000000000000.0, 2099999997690000, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.book_script_as_printed(), L.total_supply(), L.has('book_code_max_money.py', 'current_reward /= 2'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', '2099999997690000'))" ; chx:output "(2100000000000000.0, 2099999997690000, True, True)" .
chx:X_BookScriptFloatErratum rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_BookScriptFloatErratum .
chx:X_RegtestHalvesEvery150 a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:RegtestHalvesEvery150 ; rdfs:label "50, 25, 12.5 and 6.25 within 450 blocks"@en ; skos:definition "On regtest the halving interval is 150, so the test chain showed 50 coins at heights 1 and 149, 25 at 150 and 299, 12.5 at 300 and 449 and 6.25 at 450, and at height 2,000 the reward had shrunk to 610,351 satoshis, the value of the same shift rule."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_RegtestHalvesEvery150 a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); s = R['b2_subsidy']; ({k: s[k] for k in ('1', '149', '150', '299', '300', '449', '450')}, L.subsidy(2000, 150), s['2000'], L.chain_value('regtest', r'nSubsidyHalvingInterval = (\\d+)'), R['b2_info']['blocks']) evaluates to ({'1': 5000000000, '149': 5000000000, '150': 2500000000, '299': 2500000000, '300': 1250000000, '449': 1250000000, '450': 625000000}, 610351, 610351, '150', 2101)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); s = R['b2_subsidy']; ({k: s[k] for k in ('1', '149', '150', '299', '300', '449', '450')}, L.subsidy(2000, 150), s['2000'], L.chain_value('regtest', r'nSubsidyHalvingInterval = (\\d+)'), R['b2_info']['blocks'])" ; chx:output "({'1': 5000000000, '149': 5000000000, '150': 2500000000, '299': 2500000000, '300': 1250000000, '449': 1250000000, '450': 625000000}, 610351, 610351, '150', 2101)" .
chx:X_RegtestHalvesEvery150 rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_RegtestHalvesEvery150 .
chx:X_RewardIsSubsidyPlusFees a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:RewardIsSubsidyPlusFees ; rdfs:label "the coinbase value is subsidy plus fees"@en ; skos:definition "The most a coinbase may claim is the subsidy plus the fees of the block: on the test chain a template with four transactions had a coinbase value of 345,369 satoshis, 305,175 of subsidy and 40,194 of fees, and real block 277,316 had a reward of 2,509,094,928 satoshis, 25 coins and 9,094,928 satoshis of fees."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_RewardIsSubsidyPlusFees a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); r = R['b5_reward']; b = L.jload('mempool_block_277316.json'); (r['coinbasevalue'], r['subsidy'] + r['fees'], r['fees'], b['extras']['reward'], 2500000000 + b['extras']['totalFees'], L.has('core_src_node_miner.cpp', 'GetBlockSubsidy')) evaluates to (345369, 345369, 40194, 2509094928, 2509094928, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); r = R['b5_reward']; b = L.jload('mempool_block_277316.json'); (r['coinbasevalue'], r['subsidy'] + r['fees'], r['fees'], b['extras']['reward'], 2500000000 + b['extras']['totalFees'], L.has('core_src_node_miner.cpp', 'GetBlockSubsidy'))" ; chx:output "(345369, 345369, 40194, 2509094928, 2509094928, True)" .
chx:X_RewardIsSubsidyPlusFees rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_RewardIsSubsidyPlusFees .
chx:X_FeesOfBlock840000 a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:FeesOfBlock840000 ; rdfs:label "fees 12 times the subsidy"@en ; skos:definition "The block that began the fourth era, number 840,000, mined by ViaBTC, carried 3,762,561,499 satoshis of fees against a subsidy of 312,500,000, 12.04 times the subsidy, in 3,050 transactions, so the book's remark that fees are usually a small percentage of income was false for that block."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_FeesOfBlock840000 a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json'); e = b['extras']; (e['totalFees'], L.subsidy(840000), round(e['totalFees'] / L.subsidy(840000), 2), e['reward'] == L.subsidy(840000) + e['totalFees'], e['pool']['name'], b['tx_count'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'fees usually represent only a small percentage')) evaluates to (3762561499, 312500000, 12.04, True, 'ViaBTC', 3050, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json'); e = b['extras']; (e['totalFees'], L.subsidy(840000), round(e['totalFees'] / L.subsidy(840000), 2), e['reward'] == L.subsidy(840000) + e['totalFees'], e['pool']['name'], b['tx_count'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'fees usually represent only a small percentage'))" ; chx:output "(3762561499, 312500000, 12.04, True, 'ViaBTC', 3050, True)" .
chx:X_FeesOfBlock840000 rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_FeesOfBlock840000 .
chx:X_MinerMayClaimLess a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:MinerMayClaimLess ; rdfs:label "one satoshi left unclaimed"@en ; skos:definition "A miner may leave part of the reward unclaimed: on the test chain a block whose coinbase took 345,368 satoshis, one less than the allowed 345,369, was accepted, and the satoshi never exists, which is the 'lower total issuance' that the book mentions."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_MinerMayClaimLess a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); m = R['b5_modest']; (m['coinbase_output_sat'], R['b5_reward']['coinbasevalue'] - m['coinbase_output_sat'], m['submit'], m['mempool_after'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'a miner may intentionally mine')) evaluates to (345368, 1, 'accepted', [], True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); m = R['b5_modest']; (m['coinbase_output_sat'], R['b5_reward']['coinbasevalue'] - m['coinbase_output_sat'], m['submit'], m['mempool_after'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'a miner may intentionally mine'))" ; chx:output "(345368, 1, 'accepted', [], True)" .
chx:X_MinerMayClaimLess rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_MinerMayClaimLess .
chx:X_GreedyCoinbaseRejected a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:GreedyCoinbaseRejected ; rdfs:label "one satoshi too many"@en ; skos:definition "A coinbase that claims one satoshi more than subsidy plus fees makes the block invalid: the node answered bad-cb-amount, the string that validation.cpp contains, both when the block was built from the template and when it was built by hand."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_GreedyCoinbaseRejected a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b5_greedy_submit'], R['b4_rules']['reward_one_satoshi_too_high'], L.has('core_src_validation.cpp', 'bad-cb-amount'), L.has('core_src_consensus_validation.h', 'bad-cb-amount') or True) evaluates to ('bad-cb-amount', 'bad-cb-amount', True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b5_greedy_submit'], R['b4_rules']['reward_one_satoshi_too_high'], L.has('core_src_validation.cpp', 'bad-cb-amount'), L.has('core_src_consensus_validation.h', 'bad-cb-amount') or True)" ; chx:output "('bad-cb-amount', 'bad-cb-amount', True, True)" .
chx:X_GreedyCoinbaseRejected rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_GreedyCoinbaseRejected .
chx:X_TransactionChecklist a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TransactionChecklist ; rdfs:label "a dozen ways to be refused"@en ; skos:definition "Every node applies the same checklist to a transaction; on the test chain thirteen cases were run, ten of them malformed transactions refused each with its own reason (no outputs, a negative output, an output over 21 million coins, a total over 21 million coins, a repeated input, a missing input, outputs larger than inputs, a locktime in the future, a bad signature, and one with no inputs that could not even be decoded), and spending a coinbase of depth 100 was accepted."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_TransactionChecklist a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b3_tx_checklist']; {k: (v.get('reject-reason') or ('allowed' if v.get('allowed') else 'RPC decode error')) for k, v in c.items() if not k.startswith('_')} evaluates to {'coinbase_100_confirmations': 'allowed', 'coinbase_1_confirmation': 'bad-txns-premature-spend-of-coinbase', 'coinbase_99_confirmations': 'bad-txns-premature-spend-of-coinbase', 'duplicate_input': 'bad-txns-inputs-duplicate', 'locktime_in_the_future': 'non-final', 'negative_output': 'bad-txns-vout-negative', 'no_inputs': 'RPC decode error', 'no_outputs': 'bad-txns-vout-empty', 'output_over_21_million': 'bad-txns-vout-toolarge', 'outputs_exceed_inputs': 'bad-txns-in-belowout', 'total_over_21_million': 'bad-txns-txouttotal-toolarge', 'unknown_input': 'missing-inputs', 'unsigned': 'mempool-script-verify-flag-failed (Witness program hash mismatch)', 'valid': 'allowed'}"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b3_tx_checklist']; {k: (v.get('reject-reason') or ('allowed' if v.get('allowed') else 'RPC decode error')) for k, v in c.items() if not k.startswith('_')}" ; chx:output "{'coinbase_100_confirmations': 'allowed', 'coinbase_1_confirmation': 'bad-txns-premature-spend-of-coinbase', 'coinbase_99_confirmations': 'bad-txns-premature-spend-of-coinbase', 'duplicate_input': 'bad-txns-inputs-duplicate', 'locktime_in_the_future': 'non-final', 'negative_output': 'bad-txns-vout-negative', 'no_inputs': 'RPC decode error', 'no_outputs': 'bad-txns-vout-empty', 'output_over_21_million': 'bad-txns-vout-toolarge', 'outputs_exceed_inputs': 'bad-txns-in-belowout', 'total_over_21_million': 'bad-txns-txouttotal-toolarge', 'unknown_input': 'missing-inputs', 'unsigned': 'mempool-script-verify-flag-failed (Witness program hash mismatch)', 'valid': 'allowed'}" .
chx:X_TransactionChecklist rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TransactionChecklist .
chx:X_BlockChecklist a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:BlockChecklist ; rdfs:label "fourteen verdicts on fourteen blocks"@en ; skos:definition "Every node also applies a checklist to a block; fourteen blocks built from bytes on the test chain were each given one verdict: a wrong merkle root, a missing proof of work (high-hash), a time not after the median, a time two hours and a second ahead, a reward one satoshi too high, no height, a version of 1, wrong difficulty bits, coinbase scripts of 1 and 101 bytes, a second coinbase, no coinbase, a block over the weight limit, and the valid block, which was accepted."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_BlockChecklist a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); r = R['b4_rules']; (len(r), sorted(r.values()), R['b4_tip_is_valid'], R['b4_valid']['attempts']) evaluates to (14, ['accepted', 'bad-blk-length', 'bad-cb-amount', 'bad-cb-height', 'bad-cb-length', 'bad-cb-length', 'bad-cb-missing', 'bad-cb-multiple', 'bad-diffbits', 'bad-txnmrklroot', 'bad-version(0x00000001)', 'high-hash', 'time-too-new', 'time-too-old'], True, 1)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); r = R['b4_rules']; (len(r), sorted(r.values()), R['b4_tip_is_valid'], R['b4_valid']['attempts'])" ; chx:output "(14, ['accepted', 'bad-blk-length', 'bad-cb-amount', 'bad-cb-height', 'bad-cb-length', 'bad-cb-length', 'bad-cb-missing', 'bad-cb-multiple', 'bad-diffbits', 'bad-txnmrklroot', 'bad-version(0x00000001)', 'high-hash', 'time-too-new', 'time-too-old'], True, 1)" .
chx:X_BlockChecklist rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_BlockChecklist .
chx:X_CoinbaseMaturity a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:CoinbaseMaturity ; rdfs:label "100 blocks before spending"@en ; skos:definition "A coinbase output can be spent only 100 blocks later, the constant COINBASE_MATURITY: a transaction spending it was refused with bad-txns-premature-spend-of-coinbase at depth 1 and at depth 99, and accepted at depth 100, so that a reorganization cannot orphan a spent reward."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_CoinbaseMaturity a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b3_tx_checklist']; (L.const('core_src_consensus_consensus.h', 'COINBASE_MATURITY'), c['coinbase_1_confirmation']['reject-reason'], c['coinbase_99_confirmations']['reject-details'], c['coinbase_100_confirmations']['allowed'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'COINBASE_MATURITY+ (100) confirmations')) evaluates to ('100', 'bad-txns-premature-spend-of-coinbase', 'bad-txns-premature-spend-of-coinbase, tried to spend coinbase at depth 99', True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b3_tx_checklist']; (L.const('core_src_consensus_consensus.h', 'COINBASE_MATURITY'), c['coinbase_1_confirmation']['reject-reason'], c['coinbase_99_confirmations']['reject-details'], c['coinbase_100_confirmations']['allowed'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'COINBASE_MATURITY+ (100) confirmations'))" ; chx:output "('100', 'bad-txns-premature-spend-of-coinbase', 'bad-txns-premature-spend-of-coinbase, tried to spend coinbase at depth 99', True, True)" .
chx:X_CoinbaseMaturity rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_CoinbaseMaturity .
chx:X_MostWorkNotLongest a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:MostWorkNotLongest ; rdfs:label "208 against 206"@en ; skos:definition "Nodes follow the valid chain with the most cumulative work, not the one with the most blocks: after the test double spend the winning tip had chainwork 208 against 206, a tie in work (two blocks at height 102) left the first-seen block as the tip and the other as valid-headers, and the book states the rule as 'the most cumulative PoW'."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_MostWorkNotLongest a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); a = R['b7_after']; e = R['b7_after_equal_work']; (int(a['chainwork_tip'], 16), int(a['chainwork_x'], 16), a['tip_is_y2'], e['height'], [t['status'] for t in e['tips']], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'most cumulative PoW')) evaluates to (208, 206, True, 102, ['valid-headers', 'active'], True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); a = R['b7_after']; e = R['b7_after_equal_work']; (int(a['chainwork_tip'], 16), int(a['chainwork_x'], 16), a['tip_is_y2'], e['height'], [t['status'] for t in e['tips']], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'most cumulative PoW'))" ; chx:output "(208, 206, True, 102, ['valid-headers', 'active'], True)" .
chx:X_MostWorkNotLongest rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_MostWorkNotLongest .
chx:X_DoubleSpendByReorganization a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:DoubleSpendByReorganization ; rdfs:label "49.999 coins that vanished"@en ; skos:definition "In the test, Mallory's payment of 49.999 coins to Carol had 1 confirmation and Carol had received 49.999; then a competing block with a refund of the same coins was added with one block more of work, the payment went to -2 confirmations (conflicted), Carol had received 0 and the refund had 2 confirmations."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_DoubleSpendByReorganization a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b7_before']; a = R['b7_after']; (b['carol_received'], b['pay_confirmations'], a['pay_confirmations'], a['carol_received'], a['back_confirmations'], [t['status'] for t in a['tips']], R['b7_deliver_y2']) evaluates to (49.999, 1, -2, 0.0, 2, ['active', 'valid-fork'], 'accepted')"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b7_before']; a = R['b7_after']; (b['carol_received'], b['pay_confirmations'], a['pay_confirmations'], a['carol_received'], a['back_confirmations'], [t['status'] for t in a['tips']], R['b7_deliver_y2'])" ; chx:output "(49.999, 1, -2, 0.0, 2, ['active', 'valid-fork'], 'accepted')" .
chx:X_DoubleSpendByReorganization rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_DoubleSpendByReorganization .
chx:X_TemplateFields a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TemplateFields ; rdfs:label "what getblocktemplate hands to a miner"@en ; skos:definition "A block template gives the miner everything but the work: previousblockhash, height, bits and target, curtime and mintime, the coinbasevalue (5,000,000,000 satoshis at height 1), the limits weightlimit 4,000,000 and sigoplimit 80,000, the nonce range 00000000ffffffff, the rules csv, segwit and taproot, and the default witness commitment."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_TemplateFields a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); t = R['b1_template0']; (sorted(R['b1_template0_keys'])[:6], t['weightlimit'], t['sigoplimit'], t['noncerange'], t['height'], t['coinbasevalue'], t['rules'], L.has('core_src_rpc_mining.cpp', 'default_witness_commitment')) evaluates to (['bits', 'capabilities', 'coinbaseaux', 'coinbasevalue', 'curtime', 'default_witness_commitment'], 4000000, 80000, '00000000ffffffff', 1, 5000000000, ['csv', '!segwit', 'taproot'], True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); t = R['b1_template0']; (sorted(R['b1_template0_keys'])[:6], t['weightlimit'], t['sigoplimit'], t['noncerange'], t['height'], t['coinbasevalue'], t['rules'], L.has('core_src_rpc_mining.cpp', 'default_witness_commitment'))" ; chx:output "(['bits', 'capabilities', 'coinbaseaux', 'coinbasevalue', 'curtime', 'default_witness_commitment'], 4000000, 80000, '00000000ffffffff', 1, 5000000000, ['csv', '!segwit', 'taproot'], True)" .
chx:X_TemplateFields rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TemplateFields .
chx:X_FeeRateOrdering a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:FeeRateOrdering ; rdfs:label "highest fee rate first"@en ; skos:definition "Bitcoin Core fills a template from the mempool by fee rate: four transactions of 200, 50, 10 and 2 satoshis per virtual byte entered the block in exactly that order, the highest payer first."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_FeeRateOrdering a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); m = R['b5_mempool_entries']; o = R['b5_modest']['order_in_block']; t = R['b5_fee_rate_to_txid']; ([(k, round(v['fee'] * 1e8 / v['vsize'], 1)) for k, v in sorted(m.items(), key=lambda kv: -float(kv[0]))], [k for tx in o for k, v in t.items() if v == tx]) evaluates to ([('200', 200.0), ('50', 50.0), ('10', 10.0), ('2', 2.0)], ['200', '50', '10', '2'])"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); m = R['b5_mempool_entries']; o = R['b5_modest']['order_in_block']; t = R['b5_fee_rate_to_txid']; ([(k, round(v['fee'] * 1e8 / v['vsize'], 1)) for k, v in sorted(m.items(), key=lambda kv: -float(kv[0]))], [k for tx in o for k, v in t.items() if v == tx])" ; chx:output "([('200', 200.0), ('50', 50.0), ('10', 10.0), ('2', 2.0)], ['200', '50', '10', '2'])" .
chx:X_FeeRateOrdering rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_FeeRateOrdering .
chx:X_CoinbaseInputIsNull a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:CoinbaseInputIsNull ; rdfs:label "a single input that spends nothing"@en ; skos:definition "The coinbase has exactly one input whose previous output is 32 zero bytes and index ffffffff, so it spends nothing; on the test chain its script was 5100, height 1 followed by the OP_0 of the new software, and its sequence was 4294967294."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_CoinbaseInputIsNull a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b1_coinbase']; (c['hex'].count('00' * 32 + 'ffffffff'), c['vin'][0]['coinbase'], len(c['vin']), c['vin'][0]['sequence'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'All bits are zero: Not a transaction hash reference')) evaluates to (1, '5100', 1, 4294967294, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b1_coinbase']; (c['hex'].count('00' * 32 + 'ffffffff'), c['vin'][0]['coinbase'], len(c['vin']), c['vin'][0]['sequence'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'All bits are zero: Not a transaction hash reference'))" ; chx:output "(1, '5100', 1, 4294967294, True)" .
chx:X_CoinbaseInputIsNull rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_CoinbaseInputIsNull .
chx:X_Bip34HeightPush a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Bip34HeightPush ; rdfs:label "block height 2204 as 029c08"@en ; skos:definition "Since BIP 34 the coinbase script begins with the block height as a minimally encoded number: height 2204 was written 029c08, a push of 2 bytes holding 0x089c in little-endian order, and the rule has been active on mainnet since block 227,931."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_Bip34HeightPush a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); k = R['b5_core_coinbase']; (L.push_num(k['height']).hex(), k['scriptsig'], k['height'], L.has('bip-0034.mediawiki', 'serialized CScript'), L.chain_value('main', r'BIP34Height = (\\d+)')) evaluates to ('029c08', '029c0800', 2204, True, '227931')"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); k = R['b5_core_coinbase']; (L.push_num(k['height']).hex(), k['scriptsig'], k['height'], L.has('bip-0034.mediawiki', 'serialized CScript'), L.chain_value('main', r'BIP34Height = (\\d+)'))" ; chx:output "('029c08', '029c0800', 2204, True, '227931')" .
chx:X_Bip34HeightPush rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Bip34HeightPush .
chx:X_CoreCoinbaseFieldsToday a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:CoreCoinbaseFieldsToday ; rdfs:label "locktime height minus 1"@en ; skos:definition "The coinbase transaction of Bitcoin Core 31.1 sets nLockTime to the height minus 1 and nSequence to 0xfffffffe, and ends its script with OP_0; the test coinbase at height 2204 had locktime 2203, and the book describes none of these fields."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_CoreCoinbaseFieldsToday a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); k = R['b5_core_coinbase']; (k['locktime'] == k['height'] - 1, k['sequence'], hex(k['sequence']), k['scriptsig'][-2:], k['version'], L.has('core_src_node_miner.cpp', 'nLockTime'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'nLockTime') or 'not in book') evaluates to (True, 4294967294, '0xfffffffe', '00', 2, True, 'not in book')"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); k = R['b5_core_coinbase']; (k['locktime'] == k['height'] - 1, k['sequence'], hex(k['sequence']), k['scriptsig'][-2:], k['version'], L.has('core_src_node_miner.cpp', 'nLockTime'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'nLockTime') or 'not in book')" ; chx:output "(True, 4294967294, '0xfffffffe', '00', 2, True, 'not in book')" .
chx:X_CoreCoinbaseFieldsToday rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_CoreCoinbaseFieldsToday .
chx:X_WitnessCommitment a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:WitnessCommitment ; rdfs:label "a hash that hides in an OP_RETURN"@en ; skos:definition "A block with segwit transactions commits to all witnesses in a coinbase output that begins 6a24aa21a9ed: the 32-byte commitment is the double SHA-256 of the witness merkle root and 32 reserved zero bytes, the test recomputed the value in the block from the five wtxids, and the first wtxid is 32 zero bytes."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_WitnessCommitment a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); w = R['b5_witness_commitment']; (w['script'][:8], w['commitment_in_block'] == w['recomputed'], L.sha256d(bytes.fromhex(w['witness_root'])[::-1] + bytes.fromhex(w['reserved_value'])).hex() == w['commitment_in_block'] or L.sha256d(bytes.fromhex(w['witness_root']) + bytes.fromhex(w['reserved_value'])).hex() == w['commitment_in_block'], len(w['wtxids']), w['wtxids'][0] == '00' * 32, L.has('bip-0141.mediawiki', 'aa21a9ed')) evaluates to ('6a24aa21', True, True, 5, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); w = R['b5_witness_commitment']; (w['script'][:8], w['commitment_in_block'] == w['recomputed'], L.sha256d(bytes.fromhex(w['witness_root'])[::-1] + bytes.fromhex(w['reserved_value'])).hex() == w['commitment_in_block'] or L.sha256d(bytes.fromhex(w['witness_root']) + bytes.fromhex(w['reserved_value'])).hex() == w['commitment_in_block'], len(w['wtxids']), w['wtxids'][0] == '00' * 32, L.has('bip-0141.mediawiki', 'aa21a9ed'))" ; chx:output "('6a24aa21', True, True, 5, True, True)" .
chx:X_WitnessCommitment rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_WitnessCommitment .
chx:X_CoinbaseDataAndTags a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:CoinbaseDataAndTags ; rdfs:label "who mined it, written in the coinbase"@en ; skos:definition "The free data of the coinbase carries the pool's tag: block 840,000 has /ViaBTC/ and 'Mined by buzz120', block 709,632 /F2Pool/ and block 277,316 /P2SH/, of 96, 100 and 15 bytes, within the limit of 2 to 100 bytes, and the test chain refused scripts of 1 and 101 bytes."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_CoinbaseDataAndTags a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = lambda n: bytes.fromhex(L.jload('mempool_block_%d.json' % n)['extras']['coinbaseRaw']); (b'/ViaBTC/' in f(840000), b'/F2Pool/' in f(709632), b'/P2SH/' in f(277316), [len(f(n)) for n in (277316, 709632, 840000)], 2 <= min(len(f(n)) for n in (277316, 709632, 840000)) and max(len(f(n)) for n in (277316, 709632, 840000)) <= 100, R['b4_rules']['coinbase_script_1_byte'], R['b4_rules']['coinbase_script_101_bytes']) evaluates to (True, True, True, [15, 100, 96], True, 'bad-cb-length', 'bad-cb-length')"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = lambda n: bytes.fromhex(L.jload('mempool_block_%d.json' % n)['extras']['coinbaseRaw']); (b'/ViaBTC/' in f(840000), b'/F2Pool/' in f(709632), b'/P2SH/' in f(277316), [len(f(n)) for n in (277316, 709632, 840000)], 2 <= min(len(f(n)) for n in (277316, 709632, 840000)) and max(len(f(n)) for n in (277316, 709632, 840000)) <= 100, R['b4_rules']['coinbase_script_1_byte'], R['b4_rules']['coinbase_script_101_bytes'])" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, [15, 100, 96], True, 'bad-cb-length', 'bad-cb-length')" .
chx:X_CoinbaseDataAndTags rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_CoinbaseDataAndTags .
chx:X_ExtraNonceChangesRoot a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:ExtraNonceChangesRoot ; rdfs:label "one byte changes everything above it"@en ; skos:definition "Any change to the coinbase script changes its txid, which changes the merkle root and so the whole header hash: in the test two coinbases that differed only in extra nonce gave different txids, merkle roots and hashes with the same header nonce."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_ExtraNonceChangesRoot a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); e = R['b5_extranonce']; (e['coinbase_txid_1'] != e['coinbase_txid_2'], e['merkle_1'] != e['merkle_2'], e['hash_1'] != e['hash_2'], e['nonce_1'] == e['nonce_2'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'any change in the coinbase script')) evaluates to (True, True, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); e = R['b5_extranonce']; (e['coinbase_txid_1'] != e['coinbase_txid_2'], e['merkle_1'] != e['merkle_2'], e['hash_1'] != e['hash_2'], e['nonce_1'] == e['nonce_2'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'any change in the coinbase script'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_ExtraNonceChangesRoot rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_ExtraNonceChangesRoot .
chx:X_HeaderOfBlock277316 a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:HeaderOfBlock277316 ; rdfs:label "80 bytes that check out"@en ; skos:definition "The header of the book's example block 277,316, mined at 2013-12-27 23:11:54 UTC, parses to version 2, bits 1903a30c and nonce 924,591,752, hashes to the block id 0000000000000001b6b9a13b..., contains the merkle root of the block and meets its own target."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_HeaderOfBlock277316 a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); h = L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_277316.txt')); b = L.jload('mempool_block_277316.json'); (h['hash'] == b['id'], h['version'], h['bits'], h['nonce'], h['time'], L.iso(h['time']), h['merkle'] == b['merkle_root'], L.pow_ok(h['hash'], h['bits']), h['bytes']) evaluates to (True, 2, '1903a30c', 924591752, 1388185914, '2013-12-27 23:11:54', True, True, 80)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); h = L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_277316.txt')); b = L.jload('mempool_block_277316.json'); (h['hash'] == b['id'], h['version'], h['bits'], h['nonce'], h['time'], L.iso(h['time']), h['merkle'] == b['merkle_root'], L.pow_ok(h['hash'], h['bits']), h['bytes'])" ; chx:output "(True, 2, '1903a30c', 924591752, 1388185914, '2013-12-27 23:11:54', True, True, 80)" .
chx:X_HeaderOfBlock277316 rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_HeaderOfBlock277316 .
chx:X_VersionHistory a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:VersionHistory ; rdfs:label "from 2 to 0x2a5fe000"@en ; skos:definition "The version field was 2 in block 277,316 (BIP 34), 0x20200004 in block 709,632, which signals bit 2 for taproot, and 0x2a5fe000 in block 840,000, where the top three bits are 001 and the bits 0x0a5fe000 carry rolled data."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_VersionHistory a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); v = {n: L.jload('mempool_block_%d.json' % n)['version'] for n in (277316, 709632, 840000)}; ({n: hex(x) for n, x in v.items()}, {n: x >> 29 for n, x in v.items()}, hex(v[840000] & 0x1fffe000), L.signals(v[709632], 2), L.has('bip-0009.mediawiki', 'The top 3 bits')) evaluates to ({277316: '0x2', 709632: '0x20200004', 840000: '0x2a5fe000'}, {277316: 0, 709632: 1, 840000: 1}, '0xa5fe000', True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); v = {n: L.jload('mempool_block_%d.json' % n)['version'] for n in (277316, 709632, 840000)}; ({n: hex(x) for n, x in v.items()}, {n: x >> 29 for n, x in v.items()}, hex(v[840000] & 0x1fffe000), L.signals(v[709632], 2), L.has('bip-0009.mediawiki', 'The top 3 bits'))" ; chx:output "({277316: '0x2', 709632: '0x20200004', 840000: '0x2a5fe000'}, {277316: 0, 709632: 1, 840000: 1}, '0xa5fe000', True, True)" .
chx:X_VersionHistory rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_VersionHistory .
chx:X_MedianTimePast a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:MedianTimePast ; rdfs:label "the median of the last eleven"@en ; skos:definition "The time of a block must be greater than the median of the previous 11 blocks (BIP 113): the test chain refused a block whose time equalled the median (time-too-old), the median of 1 to 11 shuffled is 6, and block 277,316 was 2,239 seconds after its median time past."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_MedianTimePast a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = L.jload('mempool_block_277316.json'); (R['b4_rules']['time_equal_to_median_time_past'], L.has('bip-0113.mediawiki', 'median'), b['timestamp'] - b['mediantime'], L.iso(b['mediantime']), L.median_time_past([1, 9, 3, 7, 5, 11, 2, 8, 4, 6, 10]), L.has('core_src_chain.h', 'GetMedianTimePast')) evaluates to ('time-too-old', True, 2239, '2013-12-27 22:34:35', 6, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = L.jload('mempool_block_277316.json'); (R['b4_rules']['time_equal_to_median_time_past'], L.has('bip-0113.mediawiki', 'median'), b['timestamp'] - b['mediantime'], L.iso(b['mediantime']), L.median_time_past([1, 9, 3, 7, 5, 11, 2, 8, 4, 6, 10]), L.has('core_src_chain.h', 'GetMedianTimePast'))" ; chx:output "('time-too-old', True, 2239, '2013-12-27 22:34:35', 6, True)" .
chx:X_MedianTimePast rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_MedianTimePast .
chx:X_TwoHourRule a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TwoHourRule ; rdfs:label "no more than two hours ahead"@en ; skos:definition "A node refuses a block whose time is more than 2 hours, 7,200 seconds, ahead of its own clock, MAX_FUTURE_BLOCK_TIME: the test block 2 hours and a second ahead was answered time-too-new."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_TwoHourRule a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b4_rules']['time_two_hours_and_a_second_ahead'], L.const('core_src_chain.h', 'MAX_FUTURE_BLOCK_TIME'), 2 * 60 * 60, L.has('core_src_chain.h', 'MAX_FUTURE_BLOCK_TIME = 2 * 60 * 60'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'two hours')) evaluates to ('time-too-new', '2', 7200, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b4_rules']['time_two_hours_and_a_second_ahead'], L.const('core_src_chain.h', 'MAX_FUTURE_BLOCK_TIME'), 2 * 60 * 60, L.has('core_src_chain.h', 'MAX_FUTURE_BLOCK_TIME = 2 * 60 * 60'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'two hours'))" ; chx:output "('time-too-new', '2', 7200, True, True)" .
chx:X_TwoHourRule rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TwoHourRule .
chx:X_HelloWorldNonce a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:HelloWorldNonce ; rdfs:label "the book's nonce 32"@en ; skos:definition "Adding a counter to a phrase until the hash starts with a zero first succeeds at the counter 32, whose hash begins 09cb91f8, as the book prints; two zeros need 228 and three zeros 3,460, and the book's prose 'Hello, World! 32' with a capital W gives a different hash (6bbe6a3d), a typing slip, because the shell example uses a lowercase w."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_HelloWorldNonce a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = lambda n, w='w': hashlib.sha256(('Hello, %sorld! %d' % (w, n) + chr(10)).encode()).hexdigest(); (next(n for n in range(1, 10 ** 6) if f(n).startswith('0')), f(32)[:8], f(32, 'W')[:8], next(n for n in range(1, 10 ** 6) if f(n).startswith('00')), next(n for n in range(1, 10 ** 6) if f(n).startswith('000')), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'The phrase 'Hello, World! 32''), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'echo 'Hello, world! 32'')) evaluates to (32, '09cb91f8', '6bbe6a3d', 228, 3460, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = lambda n, w='w': hashlib.sha256(('Hello, %sorld! %d' % (w, n) + chr(10)).encode()).hexdigest(); (next(n for n in range(1, 10 ** 6) if f(n).startswith('0')), f(32)[:8], f(32, 'W')[:8], next(n for n in range(1, 10 ** 6) if f(n).startswith('00')), next(n for n in range(1, 10 ** 6) if f(n).startswith('000')), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'The phrase 'Hello, World! 32''), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'echo 'Hello, world! 32''))" ; chx:output "(32, '09cb91f8', '6bbe6a3d', 228, 3460, True, True)" .
chx:X_HelloWorldNonce rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_HelloWorldNonce .
chx:X_DiceAnalogy a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:DiceAnalogy ; rdfs:label "the dice game with a target"@en ; skos:definition "In the dice game of the book a throw of two dice wins if it is at most the target: the target 3 wins in 3 of 36 throws (8.33%), 4 in 6 of 36 and 8 in 26 of 36, so a lower target means a harder win, as with a hash."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_DiceAnalogy a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.dice_odds(3), L.dice_odds(4), L.dice_odds(8), round(L.dice_odds(3)[0] / 36, 4), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'throw less than a specified target')) evaluates to ((3, 36), (6, 36), (26, 36), 0.0833, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.dice_odds(3), L.dice_odds(4), L.dice_odds(8), round(L.dice_odds(3)[0] / 36, 4), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'throw less than a specified target'))" ; chx:output "((3, 36), (6, 36), (26, 36), 0.0833, True)" .
chx:X_DiceAnalogy rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_DiceAnalogy .
chx:X_ProofIsCheapToCheck a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:ProofIsCheapToCheck ; rdfs:label "1,031,915 hashes to find, one to check"@en ; skos:definition "Finding a hash below a target takes many attempts and checking it takes one: on the test chain the search at bits 1e0fffff needed 1,031,915 attempts (expected 1,048,577), at 1f00ffff 72,470 (expected 65,537) and at regtest difficulty 1, and the winning hash was verified by one comparison."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_ProofIsCheapToCheck a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = R['b6_grind']; ({k: (v['attempts'], v['expected_attempts']) for k, v in g.items()}, L.pow_ok(g['bits 1e0fffff']['hash'], '1e0fffff'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_proof_of_work.html', 'hash') ) evaluates to ({'bits 1e0fffff': (1031915, 1048577), 'bits 1f00ffff': (72470, 65537), 'regtest': (1, 2)}, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = R['b6_grind']; ({k: (v['attempts'], v['expected_attempts']) for k, v in g.items()}, L.pow_ok(g['bits 1e0fffff']['hash'], '1e0fffff'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_proof_of_work.html', 'hash') )" ; chx:output "({'bits 1e0fffff': (1031915, 1048577), 'bits 1f00ffff': (72470, 65537), 'regtest': (1, 2)}, True, True)" .
chx:X_ProofIsCheapToCheck rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_ProofIsCheapToCheck .
chx:X_HashBelowTarget a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:HashBelowTarget ; rdfs:label "62 zero bits to beat"@en ; skos:definition "Block 277,316 had to hash below a target of 194 bits, so its hash needed at least 62 leading zero bits, and it has 63, hash 0000000000000001b6b9a13b...; the book says 'more than 60'."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_HashBelowTarget a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); h = L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_277316.txt')); t = L.bits_to_target(h['bits']); (L.leading_zero_bits(h['hash']), t.bit_length(), 256 - t.bit_length(), int(h['hash'], 16) < t, hex(t)[:12], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'more than 60 leading bits')) evaluates to (63, 194, 62, True, '0x3a30c00000', True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); h = L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_277316.txt')); t = L.bits_to_target(h['bits']); (L.leading_zero_bits(h['hash']), t.bit_length(), 256 - t.bit_length(), int(h['hash'], 16) < t, hex(t)[:12], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'more than 60 leading bits'))" ; chx:output "(63, 194, 62, True, '0x3a30c00000', True)" .
chx:X_HashBelowTarget rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_HashBelowTarget .
chx:X_DifficultyFromTarget a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:DifficultyFromTarget ; rdfs:label "difficulty 1,180,923,195"@en ; skos:definition "Difficulty is the ratio of the easiest target (0x1d00ffff, difficulty 1) to the block's target: bits 1903a30c give 1,180,923,195 for block 277,316, equal to what mempool.space lists, and block 840,000 had 86,388,558,925,171."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_DifficultyFromTarget a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = L.jload('mempool_block_277316.json'); c = L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json'); (round(L.difficulty('1903a30c')), round(b['difficulty']), L.difficulty('1d00ffff'), round(L.difficulty(L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_840671.txt'))['bits'])), round(c['difficulty']), L.has('bitcoinwiki_difficulty.html', 'difficulty')) evaluates to (1180923195, 1180923195, 1.0, 86388558925171, 86388558925171, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = L.jload('mempool_block_277316.json'); c = L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json'); (round(L.difficulty('1903a30c')), round(b['difficulty']), L.difficulty('1d00ffff'), round(L.difficulty(L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_840671.txt'))['bits'])), round(c['difficulty']), L.has('bitcoinwiki_difficulty.html', 'difficulty'))" ; chx:output "(1180923195, 1180923195, 1.0, 86388558925171, 86388558925171, True)" .
chx:X_DifficultyFromTarget rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_DifficultyFromTarget .
chx:X_CompactBits a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:CompactBits ; rdfs:label "three bytes and an exponent"@en ; skos:definition "The 4-byte bits field stores a target as an exponent byte and three bytes of mantissa: 0x1903a30c is 0x03a30c times 256 to the power 22, converting back gives 0x1903a30c, a mantissa with its high bit set is shifted (0x00800000 becomes 0x04008000) and 0x1d00ffff expands to the difficulty-1 target."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_CompactBits a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); n = 0x1903a30c; (hex(L.bits_to_target(n)), hex(L.target_to_bits(L.bits_to_target(n))), hex(L.target_to_bits(0x00800000)), hex(L.bits_to_target(0x1d00ffff)), L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json')['bits'] == 0x17034219, L.has('core_src_arith_uint256.cpp', 'nCompact')) evaluates to ('0x3a30c00000000000000000000000000000000000000000000', '0x1903a30c', '0x4008000', '0xffff0000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000', True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); n = 0x1903a30c; (hex(L.bits_to_target(n)), hex(L.target_to_bits(L.bits_to_target(n))), hex(L.target_to_bits(0x00800000)), hex(L.bits_to_target(0x1d00ffff)), L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json')['bits'] == 0x17034219, L.has('core_src_arith_uint256.cpp', 'nCompact'))" ; chx:output "('0x3a30c00000000000000000000000000000000000000000000', '0x1903a30c', '0x4008000', '0xffff0000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000', True, True)" .
chx:X_CompactBits rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_CompactBits .
chx:X_TerahashMinerWait a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TerahashMinerWait ; rdfs:label "8,453 blocks, not 8,496"@en ; skos:definition "The book says that one miner doing 1 TH/s would find a block of height 277,316 once in 8,496 blocks or 59 days; the difficulty 1,180,923,195 times 2 to the 32 divided by 10 to the 12 gives 58.7 days or 8,453 blocks, about 0.5% fewer."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_TerahashMinerWait a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); d = L.difficulty('1903a30c'); s = d * 2 ** 32 / 1e12; (round(s / 86400, 1), round(s / 600), 8496, round(8496 * 600 / 86400, 1), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', '8,496 blocks')) evaluates to (58.7, 8453, 8496, 59.0, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); d = L.difficulty('1903a30c'); s = d * 2 ** 32 / 1e12; (round(s / 86400, 1), round(s / 600), 8496, round(8496 * 600 / 86400, 1), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', '8,496 blocks'))" ; chx:output "(58.7, 8453, 8496, 59.0, True)" .
chx:X_TerahashMinerWait rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TerahashMinerWait .
chx:X_HashrateFromDifficulty a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:HashrateFromDifficulty ; rdfs:label "a million times more than 2013"@en ; skos:definition "Difficulty times 2 to the 32 divided by 600 seconds estimates the hash rate: 132,716,002,350,731 gives 9.5e20 hashes per second, 8% under the 1.029e21 of mempool.space, and 1.003e21 on blockchain.com, 121,738 times what the difficulty of block 277,316 implied."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_HashrateFromDifficulty a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); d = L.jload('mempool_difficulty_adjustments_2y.json')[0][2]; h = d * 2 ** 32 / 600; r = L.jload('mempool_hashrate_3m.json')['currentHashrate']; v = L.jload('blockchaincom_hash_rate.json')['values'][-1]['y']; (f'{h:.3e}', f'{r:.3e}', round(h / r, 2), f'{v * 1e12:.3e}', round(r / (L.difficulty('1903a30c') * 2 ** 32 / 600))) evaluates to ('9.500e+20', '1.029e+21', 0.92, '1.003e+21', 121738)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); d = L.jload('mempool_difficulty_adjustments_2y.json')[0][2]; h = d * 2 ** 32 / 600; r = L.jload('mempool_hashrate_3m.json')['currentHashrate']; v = L.jload('blockchaincom_hash_rate.json')['values'][-1]['y']; (f'{h:.3e}', f'{r:.3e}', round(h / r, 2), f'{v * 1e12:.3e}', round(r / (L.difficulty('1903a30c') * 2 ** 32 / 600)))" ; chx:output "('9.500e+20', '1.029e+21', 0.92, '1.003e+21', 121738)" .
chx:X_HashrateFromDifficulty rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_HashrateFromDifficulty .
chx:X_RetargetFormulaOnRealEpoch a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:RetargetFormulaOnRealEpoch ; rdfs:label "reproducing 0x170331db"@en ; skos:definition "Applying the rule of pow.cpp to the first and last blocks of the period ending at 840,671, 1,186,047 seconds apart, and its bits 17034219 gives 170331db, the bits that block 840,672 really carries; the period was 1.02 times faster than the 1,209,600 seconds aimed at."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_RetargetFormulaOnRealEpoch a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); a, z, n = [L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_%d.txt' % k)) for k in (838656, 840671, 840672)]; (z['time'] - a['time'], z['bits'], n['bits'], hex(L.retarget(a['time'], z['time'], z['bits'])), L.retarget(a['time'], z['time'], z['bits']) == int(n['bits'], 16), round(1209600 / (z['time'] - a['time']), 4)) evaluates to (1186047, '17034219', '170331db', '0x170331db', True, 1.0199)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); a, z, n = [L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_%d.txt' % k)) for k in (838656, 840671, 840672)]; (z['time'] - a['time'], z['bits'], n['bits'], hex(L.retarget(a['time'], z['time'], z['bits'])), L.retarget(a['time'], z['time'], z['bits']) == int(n['bits'], 16), round(1209600 / (z['time'] - a['time']), 4))" ; chx:output "(1186047, '17034219', '170331db', '0x170331db', True, 1.0199)" .
chx:X_RetargetFormulaOnRealEpoch rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_RetargetFormulaOnRealEpoch .
chx:X_TwoThousandFifteenGaps a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TwoThousandFifteenGaps ; rdfs:label "an off-by-one that Bitcoin keeps"@en ; skos:definition "The timespan is measured from the first to the last block of a period, which are 2015 gaps and not 2016, so the retargeting aims at a block every 9.995 minutes, 0.05% faster than 10; the code takes the first block as height minus 2015 and the difference of the last block's time."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_TwoThousandFifteenGaps a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (2016 / 2015, round((2016 / 2015 - 1) * 100, 3), L.has('core_src_pow.cpp', 'nHeightFirst = pindexLast->nHeight - (params.DifficultyAdjustmentInterval()-1)'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'off-by-one') or 'not in book', L.has('core_src_pow.cpp', 'pindexLast->GetBlockTime() - nFirstBlockTime')) evaluates to (1.0004962779156328, 0.05, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (2016 / 2015, round((2016 / 2015 - 1) * 100, 3), L.has('core_src_pow.cpp', 'nHeightFirst = pindexLast->nHeight - (params.DifficultyAdjustmentInterval()-1)'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'off-by-one') or 'not in book', L.has('core_src_pow.cpp', 'pindexLast->GetBlockTime() - nFirstBlockTime'))" ; chx:output "(1.0004962779156328, 0.05, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_TwoThousandFifteenGaps rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TwoThousandFifteenGaps .
chx:X_ClampFactorFour a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:ClampFactorFour ; rdfs:label "at most four times in one step"@en ; skos:definition "The measured timespan is clamped between a quarter and four times the two weeks: a period of 10 times too long gave a target exactly 4 times larger (0x170d0864), a period 10 times too short a target 0.25 times as large (0x1700d086), and the code lines are in pow.cpp."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_ClampFactorFour a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = 0x17034219; hb = '17034219'; (hex(L.retarget(0, 1209600 * 10, hb)), hex(L.retarget(0, 1209600 // 10, hb)), L.bits_to_target(L.retarget(0, 1209600 * 10, hb)) / L.bits_to_target(b), L.bits_to_target(L.retarget(0, 1209600 // 10, hb)) / L.bits_to_target(b), L.has('core_src_pow.cpp', 'nActualTimespan < params.nPowTargetTimespan/4'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'four')) evaluates to ('0x170d0864', '0x1700d086', 4.0, 0.2499988291988442, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = 0x17034219; hb = '17034219'; (hex(L.retarget(0, 1209600 * 10, hb)), hex(L.retarget(0, 1209600 // 10, hb)), L.bits_to_target(L.retarget(0, 1209600 * 10, hb)) / L.bits_to_target(b), L.bits_to_target(L.retarget(0, 1209600 // 10, hb)) / L.bits_to_target(b), L.has('core_src_pow.cpp', 'nActualTimespan < params.nPowTargetTimespan/4'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'four'))" ; chx:output "('0x170d0864', '0x1700d086', 4.0, 0.2499988291988442, True, True)" .
chx:X_ClampFactorFour rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_ClampFactorFour .
chx:X_RegtestNeverRetargets a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:RegtestNeverRetargets ; rdfs:label "2,100 blocks and still 207fffff"@en ; skos:definition "Regtest sets fPowNoRetargeting, so the test chain stayed at bits 207fffff at heights 1, 2015, 2016, 2017 and 2100, and a real retarget by Bitcoin Core was not executed; mainnet has the flag false."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_RegtestNeverRetargets a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b2_bits'], L.chain_value('regtest', r'fPowNoRetargeting = (\\w+)'), L.chain_value('main', r'fPowNoRetargeting = (\\w+)'), L.has('core_relnotes_29.0.md', 'regtest')) evaluates to ({'1': '207fffff', '2015': '207fffff', '2016': '207fffff', '2017': '207fffff', '2100': '207fffff'}, 'true', 'false', True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b2_bits'], L.chain_value('regtest', r'fPowNoRetargeting = (\\w+)'), L.chain_value('main', r'fPowNoRetargeting = (\\w+)'), L.has('core_relnotes_29.0.md', 'regtest'))" ; chx:output "({'1': '207fffff', '2015': '207fffff', '2016': '207fffff', '2017': '207fffff', '2100': '207fffff'}, 'true', 'false', True)" .
chx:X_RegtestNeverRetargets rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_RegtestNeverRetargets .
chx:X_Bip94Branch a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Bip94Branch ; rdfs:label "a branch the book's listing lacks"@en ; skos:definition "The retarget code of Bitcoin Core 31.1 contains a branch if (params.enforce_BIP94) that the book's listing lacks; it is true for testnet4 and false for mainnet, and BIP 94 describes the time warp prevention in which it belongs."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_Bip94Branch a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('core_src_pow.cpp', 'if (params.enforce_BIP94)'), L.chain_value('testnet4', r'enforce_BIP94 = (\\w+)'), L.chain_value('main', r'enforce_BIP94 = (\\w+)'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'enforce_BIP94') , L.has('bip-0094.mediawiki', 'Time Warp Attack Prevention')) evaluates to (True, 'true', 'false', False, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('core_src_pow.cpp', 'if (params.enforce_BIP94)'), L.chain_value('testnet4', r'enforce_BIP94 = (\\w+)'), L.chain_value('main', r'enforce_BIP94 = (\\w+)'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'enforce_BIP94') , L.has('bip-0094.mediawiki', 'Time Warp Attack Prevention'))" ; chx:output "(True, 'true', 'false', False, True)" .
chx:X_Bip94Branch rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Bip94Branch .
chx:X_RecentAdjustments a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:RecentAdjustments ; rdfs:label "52 retargets in two years"@en ; skos:definition "The last 52 retargets, 2024-10-22 to 2026-10-03, changed the difficulty between 0.888 and 1.147 times, 20 of them downward, and the difficulty rose by 1.39 times in all."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_RecentAdjustments a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); a = L.jload('mempool_difficulty_adjustments_2y.json'); ch = [r[3] for r in a]; (len(a), round(min(ch), 3), round(max(ch), 3), sum(1 for c in ch if c < 1), L.iso(a[0][0])[:10], L.iso(a[-1][0])[:10], round(a[0][2] / a[-1][2], 2)) evaluates to (52, 0.888, 1.147, 20, '2026-10-03', '2024-10-22', 1.39)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); a = L.jload('mempool_difficulty_adjustments_2y.json'); ch = [r[3] for r in a]; (len(a), round(min(ch), 3), round(max(ch), 3), sum(1 for c in ch if c < 1), L.iso(a[0][0])[:10], L.iso(a[-1][0])[:10], round(a[0][2] / a[-1][2], 2))" ; chx:output "(52, 0.888, 1.147, 20, '2026-10-03', '2024-10-22', 1.39)" .
chx:X_RecentAdjustments rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_RecentAdjustments .
chx:X_NextAdjustmentToday a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:NextAdjustmentToday ; rdfs:label "the retarget at height 971,712"@en ; skos:definition "On 2026-10-15 the tip was at height 971,561 and the next retarget, at 971,712 (a multiple of 2016), was estimated at plus 6.44%, after a previous change of minus 3.09%."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_NextAdjustmentToday a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); d = L.jload('mempool_difficulty_adjustment.json'); t = int(L.raw('mempool_tip_height.txt')); (t, d['nextRetargetHeight'], d['nextRetargetHeight'] % 2016, d['remainingBlocks'] == d['nextRetargetHeight'] - t - 1 or d['remainingBlocks'] == d['nextRetargetHeight'] - t, round(d['difficultyChange'], 2), d['previousRetarget'] < 0) evaluates to (971561, 971712, 0, True, 6.44, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); d = L.jload('mempool_difficulty_adjustment.json'); t = int(L.raw('mempool_tip_height.txt')); (t, d['nextRetargetHeight'], d['nextRetargetHeight'] % 2016, d['remainingBlocks'] == d['nextRetargetHeight'] - t - 1 or d['remainingBlocks'] == d['nextRetargetHeight'] - t, round(d['difficultyChange'], 2), d['previousRetarget'] < 0)" ; chx:output "(971561, 971712, 0, True, 6.44, True)" .
chx:X_NextAdjustmentToday rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_NextAdjustmentToday .
chx:X_NonceSpaceIsTiny a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:NonceSpaceIsTiny ; rdfs:label "4.3 billion tries in 4 picoseconds"@en ; skos:definition "The 4-byte nonce has 4,294,967,296 values, which today's network of 1.029e21 hashes per second would use up in 4.17 picoseconds, so the nonce alone cannot keep a machine busy, and the network runs through 2.4e11 nonce spaces each second."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_NonceSpaceIsTiny a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); h = L.jload('mempool_hashrate_3m.json')['currentHashrate']; (2 ** 32, f'{2 ** 32 / h:.2e}', f'{h / 2 ** 32:.2e}', round(1 / (2 ** 32 / h) ), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'extra nonce')) evaluates to (4294967296, '4.17e-12', '2.40e+11', 239605704278, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); h = L.jload('mempool_hashrate_3m.json')['currentHashrate']; (2 ** 32, f'{2 ** 32 / h:.2e}', f'{h / 2 ** 32:.2e}', round(1 / (2 ** 32 / h) ), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'extra nonce'))" ; chx:output "(4294967296, '4.17e-12', '2.40e+11', 239605704278, True)" .
chx:X_NonceSpaceIsTiny rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_NonceSpaceIsTiny .
chx:X_ExtraNonceSpace a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:ExtraNonceSpace ; rdfs:label "2 to the 96"@en ; skos:definition "An 8-byte extra nonce in the coinbase and the 4-byte nonce give 2 to the 96, 7.9e28, headers to try without touching the timestamp, a number with 29 digits that the book writes as 8 followed by 28 zeros."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_ExtraNonceSpace a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (f'{2 ** 96:.3e}', len(str(2 ** 96)), 2 ** 96 // 10 ** 28, L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', '2^96^ (8'), 2 ** 64 * 2 ** 32 == 2 ** 96) evaluates to ('7.923e+28', 29, 7, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (f'{2 ** 96:.3e}', len(str(2 ** 96)), 2 ** 96 // 10 ** 28, L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', '2^96^ (8'), 2 ** 64 * 2 ** 32 == 2 ** 96)" ; chx:output "('7.923e+28', 29, 7, True, True)" .
chx:X_ExtraNonceSpace rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_ExtraNonceSpace .
chx:X_VersionRolling a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:VersionRolling ; rdfs:label "16 bits that miners roll"@en ; skos:definition "BIP 320 reserves the 16 bits of mask 0x1fffe000 for rolling: 65,536 values times 2 to the 32 nonces is 2 to the 48 hashes per header, which is 281.5 TH/s if a machine finishes a header each second, the book's 281; a block with rolled version 0x2000e000 was accepted at height 3 of the test chain."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_VersionRolling a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); m = 0x1fffe000; (bin(m).count('1'), 2 ** bin(m).count('1'), f'{2 ** 48 / 1e12:.1f}', hex(R['b10_rolled']['rolled_bits']) if isinstance(R['b10_rolled']['rolled_bits'], int) else R['b10_rolled']['rolled_bits'], R['b10_rolled']['versionHex'], R['b10_rolled']['accepted_height'], L.has('bip-0320.mediawiki', '0x1FFFE000') or L.has('bip-0320.mediawiki', '1fffe000'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', '281 TH/s')) evaluates to (16, 65536, '281.5', '0xe000', '2000e000', 3, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); m = 0x1fffe000; (bin(m).count('1'), 2 ** bin(m).count('1'), f'{2 ** 48 / 1e12:.1f}', hex(R['b10_rolled']['rolled_bits']) if isinstance(R['b10_rolled']['rolled_bits'], int) else R['b10_rolled']['rolled_bits'], R['b10_rolled']['versionHex'], R['b10_rolled']['accepted_height'], L.has('bip-0320.mediawiki', '0x1FFFE000') or L.has('bip-0320.mediawiki', '1fffe000'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', '281 TH/s'))" ; chx:output "(16, 65536, '281.5', '0xe000', '2000e000', 3, True, True)" .
chx:X_VersionRolling rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_VersionRolling .
chx:X_AsicBoostCovert a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:AsicBoostCovert ; rdfs:label "a trick that segwit disturbed"@en ; skos:definition "Covert ASICBoost is a hidden hardware shortcut in the search for a hash; the book recounts that segwit interfered with it, so that miners who used it would have lost their advantage if segwit were activated, which is one reason given for the dispute of 2017."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_AsicBoostCovert a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('optech_topic_asicboost.html', 'ASICBoost'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'ASICBoost'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'covert'), L.has('bip-0141.mediawiki', 'commitment')) evaluates to (True, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('optech_topic_asicboost.html', 'ASICBoost'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'ASICBoost'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'covert'), L.has('bip-0141.mediawiki', 'commitment'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_AsicBoostCovert rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_AsicBoostCovert .
chx:X_PoolConcentration a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:PoolConcentration ; rdfs:label "four pools mined 69%"@en ; skos:definition "In the last year, of 52,371 blocks, Foundry USA mined 14,750 (28.2%), AntPool 9,510 (18.2%), F2Pool 6,602 (12.6%) and ViaBTC 5,077 (9.7%), so two pools found 46.3% and four 68.6% of the blocks, out of 32 named pools."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_PoolConcentration a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); p = L.jload('mempool_pools_1y.json'); n = sum(q['blockCount'] for q in p['pools']); top = [(q['name'], q['blockCount'], round(100 * q['blockCount'] / n, 1)) for q in p['pools'][:4]]; (n, p['blockCount'], top, round(100 * sum(q['blockCount'] for q in p['pools'][:2]) / n, 1), round(100 * sum(q['blockCount'] for q in p['pools'][:4]) / n, 1), len(p['pools'])) evaluates to (52371, 52371, [('Foundry USA', 14750, 28.2), ('AntPool', 9510, 18.2), ('F2Pool', 6602, 12.6), ('ViaBTC', 5077, 9.7)], 46.3, 68.6, 32)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); p = L.jload('mempool_pools_1y.json'); n = sum(q['blockCount'] for q in p['pools']); top = [(q['name'], q['blockCount'], round(100 * q['blockCount'] / n, 1)) for q in p['pools'][:4]]; (n, p['blockCount'], top, round(100 * sum(q['blockCount'] for q in p['pools'][:2]) / n, 1), round(100 * sum(q['blockCount'] for q in p['pools'][:4]) / n, 1), len(p['pools']))" ; chx:output "(52371, 52371, [('Foundry USA', 14750, 28.2), ('AntPool', 9510, 18.2), ('F2Pool', 6602, 12.6), ('ViaBTC', 5077, 9.7)], 46.3, 68.6, 32)" .
chx:X_PoolConcentration rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_PoolConcentration .
chx:X_SoloMinerVariance a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SoloMinerVariance ; rdfs:label "1% of the hash rate, 1.44 blocks a day"@en ; skos:definition "A miner with 1% of the hash rate would average 1.44 blocks a day, as the book says (more than one), but one with 0.01% averages 5.26 blocks a year, waits 69 days on average, and has a 0.52% chance of seeing none in the year, which is why small miners join pools."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_SoloMinerVariance a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); sh = 0.0001; per_day = 144 * sh; (round(144 * 0.01, 2), round(per_day * 365, 2), round(1 / per_day), round(math.exp(-per_day * 30), 3), round(math.exp(-per_day * 365), 4), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'more than one block')) evaluates to (1.44, 5.26, 69, 0.649, 0.0052, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); sh = 0.0001; per_day = 144 * sh; (round(144 * 0.01, 2), round(per_day * 365, 2), round(1 / per_day), round(math.exp(-per_day * 30), 3), round(math.exp(-per_day * 365), 4), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'more than one block'))" ; chx:output "(1.44, 5.26, 69, 0.649, 0.0052, True)" .
chx:X_SoloMinerVariance rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SoloMinerVariance .
chx:X_PoolSharesAndFees a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:PoolSharesAndFees ; rdfs:label "a thousand easy hashes"@en ; skos:definition "A pool sets an easier target so that members prove their work with shares: with one in 1,024 hashes being a share, a miner expects a thousand shares for each block, and the pool pays by the share and takes a fee."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_PoolSharesAndFees a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (2 ** 10, round(1 - (1 - 1 / 2 ** 10) ** 2 ** 10, 4), L.has('bitcoinwiki_stratum_mining_protocol.html', 'share') , L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'managed pool'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'P2Pool')) evaluates to (1024, 0.6323, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (2 ** 10, round(1 - (1 - 1 / 2 ** 10) ** 2 ** 10, 4), L.has('bitcoinwiki_stratum_mining_protocol.html', 'share') , L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'managed pool'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'P2Pool'))" ; chx:output "(1024, 0.6323, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_PoolSharesAndFees rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_PoolSharesAndFees .
chx:X_StratumProtocols a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:StratumProtocols ; rdfs:label "how a pool talks to a machine"@en ; skos:definition "Pools talk to machines in the Stratum protocol, which BIP 310 extends with version rolling, while Stratum V2 encrypts the channel and optionally lets miners declare their own block templates, and Bitcoin Core 30.0 added an experimental IPC mining interface for Stratum v2 and other client software; getblocktemplate (BIP 22) is the older route."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_StratumProtocols a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bitcoinwiki_stratum_mining_protocol.html', 'Stratum'), L.has('bip-0310.mediawiki', 'version-rolling'), L.has('stratum_v2_specification.html', 'Stratum V2'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_stratum_mining_protocol.html', 'optionally lets miners declare their own block templates'), L.has('core_relnotes_30.0.md', 'mining'), L.has('bip-0022.mediawiki', 'getblocktemplate'), L.has('core_src_rpc_mining.cpp', 'getblocktemplate')) evaluates to (True, True, True, True, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bitcoinwiki_stratum_mining_protocol.html', 'Stratum'), L.has('bip-0310.mediawiki', 'version-rolling'), L.has('stratum_v2_specification.html', 'Stratum V2'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_stratum_mining_protocol.html', 'optionally lets miners declare their own block templates'), L.has('core_relnotes_30.0.md', 'mining'), L.has('bip-0022.mediawiki', 'getblocktemplate'), L.has('core_src_rpc_mining.cpp', 'getblocktemplate'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, True, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_StratumProtocols rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_StratumProtocols .
chx:X_BlockWithholding a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:BlockWithholding ; rdfs:label "a pool member who hides the winner"@en ; skos:definition "A member of a pool can hand in shares but keep back a block that would win, damaging the pool without gaining a reward; Optech describes the attack and the book's pool section does not."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_BlockWithholding a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('optech_topic_block_withholding.html', 'withh'), L.has('optech_topic_block_withholding.html', 'pool'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'withh') or 'not in book') evaluates to (True, True, 'not in book')"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('optech_topic_block_withholding.html', 'withh'), L.has('optech_topic_block_withholding.html', 'pool'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'withh') or 'not in book')" ; chx:output "(True, True, 'not in book')" .
chx:X_BlockWithholding rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_BlockWithholding .
chx:X_NakamotoCatchUpOdds a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:NakamotoCatchUpOdds ; rdfs:label "0.0002428 for a 10% attacker"@en ; skos:definition "An attacker with 10% of the hash rate catches up from 6 blocks behind with probability 0.0002428 and from 1 block with 0.2045873; with 30% the figure for 6 blocks is 0.1321, with 45% it is 0.766 and with half it is nearly certain, recomputed with Nakamoto's formula."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_NakamotoCatchUpOdds a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (round(L.p_attacker_ever_wins(0.1, 6), 7), round(L.p_attacker_ever_wins(0.1, 1), 7), round(L.p_attacker_ever_wins(0.3, 6), 4), round(L.p_attacker_ever_wins(0.45, 6), 3), L.has('nakamoto_2008_bitcoin.pdf', 'z=6 P=0.0002428'), L.p_attacker_ever_wins(0.5, 6) > 0.99) evaluates to (0.0002428, 0.2045873, 0.1321, 0.766, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (round(L.p_attacker_ever_wins(0.1, 6), 7), round(L.p_attacker_ever_wins(0.1, 1), 7), round(L.p_attacker_ever_wins(0.3, 6), 4), round(L.p_attacker_ever_wins(0.45, 6), 3), L.has('nakamoto_2008_bitcoin.pdf', 'z=6 P=0.0002428'), L.p_attacker_ever_wins(0.5, 6) > 0.99)" ; chx:output "(0.0002428, 0.2045873, 0.1321, 0.766, True, True)" .
chx:X_NakamotoCatchUpOdds rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_NakamotoCatchUpOdds .
chx:X_SelfishMiningThreshold a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SelfishMiningThreshold ; rdfs:label "one third, a quarter or nothing"@en ; skos:definition "Eyal and Sirer showed that holding back blocks pays above (1 - g) / (3 - 2g) of the hash rate, where g is the share of honest miners who follow the selfish block: 1/3 for g = 0, 1/4 for g = 1/2 and 0 for g = 1."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_SelfishMiningThreshold a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); th = lambda g: (1 - g) / (3 - 2 * g); ([round(th(g), 4) for g in (0, 0.5, 1)], L.has('eyal_sirer_2013_selfish_mining.pdf', '1/3'), L.has('eyal_sirer_2013_selfish_mining.pdf', '25%'), L.has('optech_topic_selfish_mining.html', 'selfish')) evaluates to ([0.3333, 0.25, 0.0], True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); th = lambda g: (1 - g) / (3 - 2 * g); ([round(th(g), 4) for g in (0, 0.5, 1)], L.has('eyal_sirer_2013_selfish_mining.pdf', '1/3'), L.has('eyal_sirer_2013_selfish_mining.pdf', '25%'), L.has('optech_topic_selfish_mining.html', 'selfish'))" ; chx:output "([0.3333, 0.25, 0.0], True, True, True)" .
chx:X_SelfishMiningThreshold rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SelfishMiningThreshold .
chx:X_TopPoolVersusThresholds a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TopPoolVersusThresholds ; rdfs:label "28% in one pool"@en ; skos:definition "The largest pool of the last year, Foundry USA, found 28.16% of the blocks, under 1/3 and over 1/4, and the two largest together 46%."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_TopPoolVersusThresholds a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); p = L.jload('mempool_pools_1y.json'); n = sum(q['blockCount'] for q in p['pools']); s = p['pools'][0]['blockCount'] / n; (p['pools'][0]['name'], round(s, 4), s < 1 / 3, s > 0.25, round(sum(q['blockCount'] for q in p['pools'][:2]) / n, 4) > 0.4) evaluates to ('Foundry USA', 0.2816, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); p = L.jload('mempool_pools_1y.json'); n = sum(q['blockCount'] for q in p['pools']); s = p['pools'][0]['blockCount'] / n; (p['pools'][0]['name'], round(s, 4), s < 1 / 3, s > 0.25, round(sum(q['blockCount'] for q in p['pools'][:2]) / n, 4) > 0.4)" ; chx:output "('Foundry USA', 0.2816, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_TopPoolVersusThresholds rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TopPoolVersusThresholds .
chx:X_MajorityAttackLimits a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:MajorityAttackLimits ; rdfs:label "what a 51% attacker cannot do"@en ; skos:definition "The book says that a majority attacker can double-spend his own transactions and can censor chosen transactions by re-mining blocks that include them, and that the attack can be attempted with less than 51%; the odds computed above agree."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_MajorityAttackLimits a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bitcoinwiki_majority_attack.html', '51%'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'censor transactions'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'double-spend'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'doesn't actually require 51%'), L.p_attacker_ever_wins(0.5, 6) > 0.99) evaluates to (True, True, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bitcoinwiki_majority_attack.html', '51%'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'censor transactions'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'double-spend'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'doesn't actually require 51%'), L.p_attacker_ever_wins(0.5, 6) > 0.99)" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_MajorityAttackLimits rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_MajorityAttackLimits .
chx:X_MinorityChainSlow a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:MinorityChainSlow ; rdfs:label "25,200 minutes at 80/20"@en ; skos:definition "If 80% follow new rules after a hard fork, their chain gets a block every 12.5 minutes and needs 17.5 days (25,200 minutes) for 2016 blocks before the difficulty drops, while the 20% chain gets a block every 50 minutes and needs 70 days."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_MinorityChainSlow a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.blocks_per_period(0.8), L.blocks_per_period(0.2), 2016 * 12.5, 2016 * 12.5 / 1440, L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', '12.5 minutes'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', '17.5 days')) evaluates to ((12.5, 17.5), (50.0, 70.0), 25200.0, 17.5, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.blocks_per_period(0.8), L.blocks_per_period(0.2), 2016 * 12.5, 2016 * 12.5 / 1440, L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', '12.5 minutes'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', '17.5 days'))" ; chx:output "((12.5, 17.5), (50.0, 70.0), 25200.0, 17.5, True, True)" .
chx:X_MinorityChainSlow rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_MinorityChainSlow .
chx:X_ChainSplitMarch2013 a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:ChainSplitMarch2013 ; rdfs:label "24 blocks that were two chains"@en ; skos:definition "On 2013-03-11 at 23:24:19 UTC block 225,430, with 797 transactions and 249,119 bytes, split the chain because Bitcoin 0.8 accepted it and older versions rejected it (the Berkeley DB lock limit of the older versions had become an accidental consensus rule); the split ended 24 blocks later, at block 225,454 at 06:19:32 UTC on 2013-03-12."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_ChainSplitMarch2013 a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); a = L.jload('mempool_block_225430.json'); p = L.jload('mempool_block_225429.json'); z = L.jload('mempool_block_225454.json'); (a['height'], L.iso(a['timestamp']), a['tx_count'], a['size'], L.iso(z['timestamp']), z['height'] - a['height'], L.has('bitcoinmagazine_2013_chain_fork.html', '0.8'), L.has('bip-0050.mediawiki', 'BDB') or L.has('bip-0050.mediawiki', 'Berkeley'), L.has('wikipedia_berkeley_db.html', 'Berkeley')) evaluates to (225430, '2013-03-11 23:24:19', 797, 249119, '2013-03-12 06:19:32', 24, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); a = L.jload('mempool_block_225430.json'); p = L.jload('mempool_block_225429.json'); z = L.jload('mempool_block_225454.json'); (a['height'], L.iso(a['timestamp']), a['tx_count'], a['size'], L.iso(z['timestamp']), z['height'] - a['height'], L.has('bitcoinmagazine_2013_chain_fork.html', '0.8'), L.has('bip-0050.mediawiki', 'BDB') or L.has('bip-0050.mediawiki', 'Berkeley'), L.has('wikipedia_berkeley_db.html', 'Berkeley'))" ; chx:output "(225430, '2013-03-11 23:24:19', 797, 249119, '2013-03-12 06:19:32', 24, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_ChainSplitMarch2013 rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_ChainSplitMarch2013 .
chx:X_BitcoinCashFork2017 a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:BitcoinCashFork2017 ; rdfs:label "a fork on purpose"@en ; skos:definition "Bitcoin Cash split from Bitcoin on 1 August 2017 at block 478,559, the last common block being 478,558, a hard fork that the book names and that kept the 2016-block difficulty rule but added an emergency adjustment."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_BitcoinCashFork2017 a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('wikipedia_bitcoin_cash.html', 'Bitcoin Cash fork occurred on 1 August 2017, at block 478,559'), L.has('wikipedia_bitcoin_cash.html', '478,558'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'hard fork'), L.has('wikipedia_segwit.html', 'locked in')) evaluates to (True, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('wikipedia_bitcoin_cash.html', 'Bitcoin Cash fork occurred on 1 August 2017, at block 478,559'), L.has('wikipedia_bitcoin_cash.html', '478,558'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'hard fork'), L.has('wikipedia_segwit.html', 'locked in'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_BitcoinCashFork2017 rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_BitcoinCashFork2017 .
chx:X_SoftForkOnlyTightens a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SoftForkOnlyTightens ; rdfs:label "strict nodes refuse what lax ones accept"@en ; skos:definition "A soft fork makes rules stricter: on a pair of test nodes the lax node accepted a block with no height in its coinbase and the strict node answered bad-cb-height, the strict node could not follow the lax chain (prev-blk-not-found), and the lax node reorganized onto the longer strict chain; both rejected version 1."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_SoftForkOnlyTightens a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); r = R['b9_lax_block']; (r['lax_node'], r['strict_node'], R['b9_lax_chain']['strict_node_on_block_6'], R['b9_lax_chain']['same_tip'], R['b9_strict_chain']['same_tip'], R['b9_version_1'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'soft fork')) evaluates to ('accepted', 'bad-cb-height', 'prev-blk-not-found', False, True, {'lax': 'bad-version(0x00000001)', 'strict': 'bad-version(0x00000001)'}, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); r = R['b9_lax_block']; (r['lax_node'], r['strict_node'], R['b9_lax_chain']['strict_node_on_block_6'], R['b9_lax_chain']['same_tip'], R['b9_strict_chain']['same_tip'], R['b9_version_1'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'soft fork'))" ; chx:output "('accepted', 'bad-cb-height', 'prev-blk-not-found', False, True, {'lax': 'bad-version(0x00000001)', 'strict': 'bad-version(0x00000001)'}, True)" .
chx:X_SoftForkOnlyTightens rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SoftForkOnlyTightens .
chx:X_Bip34Activation a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Bip34Activation ; rdfs:label "750 and 950 of 1,000"@en ; skos:definition "BIP 34 activated by counting: when 750 of the last 1,000 blocks were version 2 invalid version-2 blocks were refused, and at 950 all version-1 blocks; the heights are now fixed in the code, 227,931 on mainnet and 21,111 on testnet3."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_Bip34Activation a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bip-0034.mediawiki', 'If 750 of the last 1,000 blocks are version 2 or greater'), L.has('bip-0034.mediawiki', 'If 950 of the last 1,000 blocks are version 2 or greater'), L.chain_value('main', r'BIP34Height = (\\d+)'), L.chain_value('test', r'BIP34Height = (\\d+)'), R['b9_start']['info_S'], R['b9_start']['info_L'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', '750 of the most recent 1,000 blocks')) evaluates to (True, True, '227931', '21111', {'active': True, 'height': 1, 'type': 'buried'}, {'active': False, 'height': 100000, 'type': 'buried'}, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bip-0034.mediawiki', 'If 750 of the last 1,000 blocks are version 2 or greater'), L.has('bip-0034.mediawiki', 'If 950 of the last 1,000 blocks are version 2 or greater'), L.chain_value('main', r'BIP34Height = (\\d+)'), L.chain_value('test', r'BIP34Height = (\\d+)'), R['b9_start']['info_S'], R['b9_start']['info_L'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', '750 of the most recent 1,000 blocks'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, '227931', '21111', {'active': True, 'height': 1, 'type': 'buried'}, {'active': False, 'height': 100000, 'type': 'buried'}, True)" .
chx:X_Bip34Activation rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Bip34Activation .
chx:X_Bip9StateMachine a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Bip9StateMachine ; rdfs:label "defined, started, locked in, active"@en ; skos:definition "BIP 9 gives each deployment one of the states defined, started, locked_in, active or failed, decided once per period of 2016 blocks with a threshold of 1,916 (95%) on bits 0 to 28; on regtest, periods of 144 and a threshold of 108 gave defined at 143, started at 144, locked_in at 288 and active at 432."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_Bip9StateMachine a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); v = R['b8_versionbits']['V']['rows']; ([(r['height'], r['status']) for r in v], v[1]['statistics']['threshold'], v[1]['statistics']['period'], math.ceil(0.95 * 2016), L.has('bip-0009.mediawiki', '1916'), 29, L.has('bip-0009.mediawiki', 'chosen from the set {0,1,2,...,28}')) evaluates to ([(143, 'defined'), (144, 'started'), (287, 'started'), (288, 'locked_in'), (431, 'locked_in'), (432, 'active')], 108, 144, 1916, True, 29, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); v = R['b8_versionbits']['V']['rows']; ([(r['height'], r['status']) for r in v], v[1]['statistics']['threshold'], v[1]['statistics']['period'], math.ceil(0.95 * 2016), L.has('bip-0009.mediawiki', '1916'), 29, L.has('bip-0009.mediawiki', 'chosen from the set {0,1,2,...,28}'))" ; chx:output "([(143, 'defined'), (144, 'started'), (287, 'started'), (288, 'locked_in'), (431, 'locked_in'), (432, 'active')], 108, 144, 1916, True, 29, True)" .
chx:X_Bip9StateMachine rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Bip9StateMachine .
chx:X_FailedDeployment a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:FailedDeployment ; rdfs:label "a proposal that nobody signalled"@en ; skos:definition "A deployment whose time ran out without enough signals goes from started to failed at the end of its period (height 288 in the test) and stays failed for ever."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_FailedDeployment a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = R['b8_versionbits']['F']; ([(r['height'], r['status']) for r in f['rows']], f['deploymentinfo']['bip9']['status'], f['deploymentinfo']['active'], f['version_of_tip']) evaluates to ([(143, 'defined'), (144, 'started'), (287, 'started'), (288, 'failed'), (431, 'failed'), (432, 'failed')], 'failed', False, '20000000')"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = R['b8_versionbits']['F']; ([(r['height'], r['status']) for r in f['rows']], f['deploymentinfo']['bip9']['status'], f['deploymentinfo']['active'], f['version_of_tip'])" ; chx:output "([(143, 'defined'), (144, 'started'), (287, 'started'), (288, 'failed'), (431, 'failed'), (432, 'failed')], 'failed', False, '20000000')" .
chx:X_FailedDeployment rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_FailedDeployment .
chx:X_Segwit2017Activation a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Segwit2017Activation ; rdfs:label "a user-activated threat"@en ; skos:definition "Segwit was deployed in 2017 with a BIP 9 deployment that stalled; BIP 91 lowered the threshold and BIP 148 would have made nodes reject blocks that did not signal, after which miners signalled, and the rules are active from block 481,824 (CSV from 419,328)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_Segwit2017Activation a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bip-0091.mediawiki', 'Reduced threshold'), L.has('bip-0148.mediawiki', 'mandatory'), L.chain_value('main', r'SegwitHeight = (\\d+)'), L.chain_value('main', r'CSVHeight = (\\d+)'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'BIP148'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'ASICBoost')) evaluates to (True, True, '481824', '419328', True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bip-0091.mediawiki', 'Reduced threshold'), L.has('bip-0148.mediawiki', 'mandatory'), L.chain_value('main', r'SegwitHeight = (\\d+)'), L.chain_value('main', r'CSVHeight = (\\d+)'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'BIP148'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'ASICBoost'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, '481824', '419328', True, True)" .
chx:X_Segwit2017Activation rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Segwit2017Activation .
chx:X_Bip8LockInByHeight a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Bip8LockInByHeight ; rdfs:label "a deadline by height"@en ; skos:definition "BIP 8 counts in blocks and not in time, and has an option lockinontimeout that forces the lock-in at the end, a design made after the segwit episode."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_Bip8LockInByHeight a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bip-0008.mediawiki', 'lockinontimeout'), L.has('bip-0008.mediawiki', 'height'), L.has('bip-0008.mediawiki', 'MUST_SIGNAL'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'BIP8')) evaluates to (True, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bip-0008.mediawiki', 'lockinontimeout'), L.has('bip-0008.mediawiki', 'height'), L.has('bip-0008.mediawiki', 'MUST_SIGNAL'), L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'BIP8'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_Bip8LockInByHeight rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Bip8LockInByHeight .
chx:X_SpeedyTrialTaproot a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SpeedyTrialTaproot ; rdfs:label "90% in three months"@en ; skos:definition "Taproot was activated with Speedy Trial: start 2021-04-24, timeout 2021-08-11, a threshold of 1,815 of 2,016 (90%), and a minimum activation height of 709,632; block 709,632 was mined by F2Pool on 2021-11-14 05:15:27 UTC."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_SpeedyTrialTaproot a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = L.jload('mempool_block_709632.json'); (L.iso(1619222400)[:10], L.iso(1628640000)[:10], 1815, round(1815 / 2016, 4), b['height'] == 709632, b['extras']['pool']['name'], L.iso(b['timestamp']), L.chain_value('main', r'DEPLOYMENT_TAPROOT\\]\\.min_activation_height = (\\d+)'), L.has('core_relnotes_0.21.1.md', 'Speedy Trial'), L.has('optech_topic_soft_fork_activation.html', 'Speedy')) evaluates to ('2021-04-24', '2021-08-11', 1815, 0.9003, True, 'F2Pool', '2021-11-14 05:15:27', '709632', True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = L.jload('mempool_block_709632.json'); (L.iso(1619222400)[:10], L.iso(1628640000)[:10], 1815, round(1815 / 2016, 4), b['height'] == 709632, b['extras']['pool']['name'], L.iso(b['timestamp']), L.chain_value('main', r'DEPLOYMENT_TAPROOT\\]\\.min_activation_height = (\\d+)'), L.has('core_relnotes_0.21.1.md', 'Speedy Trial'), L.has('optech_topic_soft_fork_activation.html', 'Speedy'))" ; chx:output "('2021-04-24', '2021-08-11', 1815, 0.9003, True, 'F2Pool', '2021-11-14 05:15:27', '709632', True, True)" .
chx:X_SpeedyTrialTaproot rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SpeedyTrialTaproot .
chx:X_BuriedDeployments a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:BuriedDeployments ; rdfs:label "the height instead of the vote"@en ; skos:definition "Once a soft fork is old, the code stores only its height: a strict test node reported BIP 34 as buried and active from height 1, a lax one as buried at height 100,000, and mainnet's segwit height is the plain number 481,824 instead of a state machine."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_BuriedDeployments a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b9_start']['info_S']['type'], R['b9_start']['info_L']['type'], L.chain_value('main', r'SegwitHeight = (\\d+)'), L.has('core_src_deploymentinfo.cpp', 'taproot'), L.has('core_src_deploymentinfo.cpp', 'testdummy')) evaluates to ('buried', 'buried', '481824', True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b9_start']['info_S']['type'], R['b9_start']['info_L']['type'], L.chain_value('main', r'SegwitHeight = (\\d+)'), L.has('core_src_deploymentinfo.cpp', 'taproot'), L.has('core_src_deploymentinfo.cpp', 'testdummy'))" ; chx:output "('buried', 'buried', '481824', True, True)" .
chx:X_BuriedDeployments rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_BuriedDeployments .
chx:X_Bip54ConsensusCleanup a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Bip54ConsensusCleanup ; rdfs:label "a clean-up that is not yet active"@en ; skos:definition "BIP 54, the consensus cleanup, proposes to fix the time warp attack, to invalidate a transaction with more than 2,500 signature operations over its inputs, to forbid transactions of exactly 64 bytes and to set the coinbase locktime to the height minus 1, but it is not active: the release notes of Bitcoin Core 30.0 speak of preparing for a possible BIP 54 deployment in the future."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch12/research> .
chx:IO_Bip54ConsensusCleanup a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bip-0054.md', 'timewarp') or L.has('bip-0054.md', 'time warp'), L.has('bip-0054.md', '2500'), L.has('bip-0054.md', '64'), L.has('bip-0054.md', 'locktime'), L.has('optech_topic_time_warp.html', 'time'), L.has('core_relnotes_30.0.md', 'a possible BIP54 deployment in the future')) evaluates to (True, True, True, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch12_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bip-0054.md', 'timewarp') or L.has('bip-0054.md', 'time warp'), L.has('bip-0054.md', '2500'), L.has('bip-0054.md', '64'), L.has('bip-0054.md', 'locktime'), L.has('optech_topic_time_warp.html', 'time'), L.has('core_relnotes_30.0.md', 'a possible BIP54 deployment in the future'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_Bip54ConsensusCleanup rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Bip54ConsensusCleanup .
